<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Áncash Region</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Áncash is a region of north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, stretching from the Pacific coast to the Cordillera Blanca, whose peak Huascarán is the highest in the country. Its highland valleys were home to the Chavín culture, centred on Chavín de Huántar, and later to the Recuay culture. In 1970 an earthquake set off an avalanche from Huascarán that buried the town of Yungay.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ancash-region.jpg" alt="Áncash Region" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ondando · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nevado_Huascar%C3%A1n3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
